//? Title: Selection sort: actual minimum scans and non-self swaps
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sort integer keys by selecting the first minimum of each remaining suffix.
Actual native pass records precede the original [5,3,8,1,9,2,7] example and the
complete seeded forty-size study.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

After pass i, the prefix contains the i+1 smallest values in nondecreasing
order; choosing the minimum remaining value preserves the invariant. Exactly
n(n-1)/2 comparisons occur, regardless of input order. At most n-1 non-self
swaps occur; sorted inputs use zero. This is an unstable sort. A bound on swaps
is not a universal proof of minimum writes, especially with duplicates or when
comparing other sorting methods. The native producer records actual operations
rather than plotting an analytical curve as measured work.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/selection_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/selection_sort.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::selection_sort_trace({3, 1, 2});
    std::print("| position | actual minimum index | minimum | swapped | actual array after |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.position,
                   s.minimum_index, s.minimum, s.swapped, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Input [3,1,2]");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual comparisons {}", r.comparisons));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual swaps {}, output {}", r.swaps,
                                     r.values));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/selection_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
